※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4537

※ A reference that allows writing is a way to write the place, so the place has
※ to be one the program could have written where it stands.  A name defined
※ without `mut` is not one of those, and asking for `&mut` of it is asking to
※ get round its definition.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 1u8
    let r: &mut u8 = &mut n
    let m: u8 = r⌖
    0u6
